[
	# XIME Terminal, System Overview

	XIME.Terminal is the terminal emulation system of the XIME framework for the Elarion ecosystem. It combines a high-performance native PTY layer, the complete Termux terminal engine (VT/xterm emulation, Unicode/wcwidth, circular buffer, gesture & text selection cursor controllers), background services, and glassy themed views with extra keys support.

	## Termux Engine Externs (`externs.termux`)
	Loc: `src/main/java/externs/termux`, `src/main/cpp/externs/termux`

	* **externs.termux.terminal**, Complete Termux VT/xterm emulator, packed terminal screen buffers, `ByteQueue`, `KeyHandler`, `TextStyle`, `TerminalColorScheme`, and PTY JNI bridge.
	* **externs.termux.view**, Termux view rendering pipeline (`TerminalRenderer`), text selection cursor controllers (`TextSelectionCursorController`, `TextSelectionHandleView`), and gestures (`GestureAndScaleRecognizer`).
	* **termux.c**, Native subprocess forkpty, UTF-8 termios setup, window resizing, and process lifecycle bridge compiled directly into `libxime-terminal.so`.

	## XIME Extension Layer (`xime.terminal.*`)
	Loc: `src/main/java/xime/terminal`

	* **xime.terminal.session.TerminalSession**, XIME session lifecycle, connecting Termux terminal streams with `BackgroundZenith` async thread pools and XIME callbacks.
	* **xime.terminal.view.TerminalView**, XIME terminal container view integrating `ThemeManager`, `BatchRenderingZenith` frame coalescing, and Termux rendering.
	* **xime.terminal.view.ExtraKeysRow**, Extra keys bar (Esc, Tab, Ctrl, Alt, Arrow keys) dispatched directly to active sessions.
	* **xime.terminal.service.TerminalService**, Android foreground service managing multi-session lifecycles in the background.
	* **xime.terminal.bootstrap.ShellBootstrap**, Shell executable bootstrapping and permission manager.
	* **xime.terminal.IntegrationExample**, Usage demonstration for activity integration.
]
